  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed a 104-minute set at the Bijou Theatre on September 21, 2022, captured in a matrix recording that blends soundboard audio with audience microphones [1]. Taped and transferred by lmgbtapes, this is the only available recording of the show, which marks the 353rd entry in the archive’s collection for the band [1][2]. The setlist spans twenty-two songs, drawing from albums like Bleed Out, Tallahassee, and Getting Into Knives, while also including the unreleased track “Poltergeist” [1]. Notably, “Poltergeist” appeared after a 1,774-day absence from archived shows, making it a rare occurrence with only ten previous performances on record [2]. The band also performed “Bones Don't Rust” and “No Children,” each accompanied by spoken introductions or stories [2]. The sit-down theater format allowed for a relatively optimal front-of-house setup, resulting in consistent audio quality despite lower audience energy [1]. The recording includes a custom thumbnail created by the taping artist’s wife, thegemthecolor [1]. This performance follows a show at Saturn the previous day [2]. Listeners can expect a steady, well-documented live experience that highlights both classic material and deeper cuts from the band’s catalog [1][2].",
